From: richie-rich90454 <rjiang880@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 0009/0014] Replace account auth with OIDC to the control plane

This patch strips the Microsoft and GitHub account authentication:
both built-in auth extensions are deleted, the server no longer
injects github-authentication into web client sessions, and the web
client drops the github-only session seeding and callback special
case. Session auth moves to the gateway-issued token verified through
the server connection-token handshake configured in patch 0012; the
control plane mints short-lived signed tokens (iss
https://code.example.com, sub user-uuid, aud jahaziel-code-server,
15 minute TTL, jti session-uuid, wid workspace-uuid, scope
workspace:read workspace:write).

Touches:
  - extensions/microsoft-authentication (deleted)
  - extensions/github-authentication (deleted)
  - server web client builtin list
  - web client auth session seeding and callback route

Verification: session-auth smoke test with a gateway-issued token.

